module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.shared_precondition_re_derived_once_per_claim_frame

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data shared_precondition_re_derived_once_per_claim_frame: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "shared_precondition_re_derived_once_per_claim_frame" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**one pure precondition re-derived once per isolated claim frame, so a cost gate adjudicates the duplication and every disposition it offers is aimed at the wrong quantity** (INVALID STATE: N claims in one file each rebuild the same pure value because the evaluator memoizes within a claim and not across claims, so the gate measures N copies of a shared derivation attributed to N separate rows. The rows then read as individually expensive when the file is collectively duplicated, and DESIGN section 2 already rules on the shape -- several demands with a shared-state least common ancestor are authored duplication, to be carried or shared at that ancestor, never cached and never re-homed. HARM: the gate's refusal is true and its SUBJECT is wrong, so it misdirects every reader who trusts it. The dispositions a cost refusal makes available -- trim the subject, move it to a lane that allows the cost, widen the line -- all price the duplication as though it were the claim's work, and the two correct moves are invisible because neither is a cost decision at all. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, AND IT IS THE ONE MEASUREMENT THAT LOCATES THE CLASS: partition the claim and compare its OWN work against its precondition. Here the ladder read bare ingest of one four-line synthetic source at ~725ms, ingest plus prepare at 1106ms, and the claim's own act -- native_test_eval_one -- at ~24ms. A row whose own work is three percent of its measured cost is not an expensive claim; it is a cheap claim behind a shared precondition, and the ratio is the tell. ",

    "THE SECOND HALF OF THE CLASS IS ABOUT THE CEILING, and it is what makes this more than one file's defect: a per-claim line is derived from the corpus that was paying it, and a newly arrived claim family paying a cost kind NO incumbent pays is adjudicated by a constant that never saw it. Measured on the specimen: 3,592 planned identities pass the 500ms line precisely because none of them pays per-claim ingest, so the corpus the figure was calibrated against could not have exposed the gap. The arrival is invisible to the ceiling's own justification. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a cost gate refuses a NEW family of rows that arrived together, do not first ask how to make the cost allowed -- ask WHETHER THE SAME WORK IS BEING DONE ONCE PER ROW, by partitioning one row into its precondition and its own act. If the precondition dominates and is pure, the refusal is reporting duplication and the repair is to share the value at the seam where it is already resolved. The reviewer tell that the wrong question was asked: a proposal that trims the fixture, re-homes the rows to a looser lane, or raises the line, with no statement anywhere of how many times the precondition is computed. ",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST THREE NEIGHBOURS, because the resemblance is close in each case and the repairs do not transfer. It is NOT `right_censored_cost_read_as_exact`: there a preempted figure is read as a cost, which is a defect in the CARRIER, and it can be fixed while the duplication stands -- indeed the specimen exhibited both, and correcting the reading of cpu_at_least would have left all four rows refusing. It is NOT `ceiling_never_exercised_for_a_population_the_census_cannot_plan`: those identities are never planned, so their bound is unevaluated, whereas these were planned, executed and interrupted -- the bound was exercised and the verdict it produced was unreachable. And it is NOT the near-line family where a threshold is MISPLACED through a cluster: these rows sat 2.2x to 2.7x out, so no defensible placement of the line admits them, which is what rules out tuning as a repair and is the positive argument that the cost is structural rather than marginal. ",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#10882 and gunbc#10992. #10882 landed src/v2/test/native_decl_selection_test.dag into the required floor at 2026-09-10T20:53Z; its four witnesses each called collision_prepared, so the seed tokenized and parsed ~230 characters of synthetic source once per claim. required-witnesses-floor refused on main for nearly an hour with the summary claims_failed=0 interrupted_before_verdict=4 interrupted_cpu_deadline=4 -- NOTHING FAILING and the lane red, because an unreached verdict is fail-closed. Marginal CPU measured by claim_batch: 1113, 1330, 1375 and 1362ms against the 500ms line. #10992 repaired it by sharing the fixture at the resolved seam so the ingest is paid once, and the four rows fit. ",

    "WHAT THE DIAGNOSTIC OFFERED AND WHY BOTH ARMS WERE WRONG, recorded because two readers took them in turn and neither questioned the frame. The refusal named exactly two remedies -- reduce the cost, or move the row to a lane declaring its own ceiling -- and a cost ladder showed the first unreachable, since the cheapest possible precondition was already 1.45x the line. That made the second arm look forced, and it is worse than it looks: the only off-floor home in the tree is a namespace the floor's own authority describes as NOT COVERED by anything, so routing there would have executed the rows nowhere and greened the gate over four unobserved claims. A diagnostic that enumerates its remedies teaches its reader that the enumeration is exhaustive; here the repair was in neither arm, and the reason is that both arms are about what the cost is ALLOWED to be while the defect was how many times it was paid. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The gate refuses, typed and located, and contains the harm -- it did not ship a wrong verdict. What it does not do is name the duplication, so the refusal is discovered per family and diagnosed by hand, and on this specimen two readers in sequence reasoned about cost allowance before anyone asked about cost multiplicity. ",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, and it is bounded there rather than higher for a reason worth stating. Whether one pure derivation is reached from several claim frames is decidable from the resolved graph -- the demands, their least common ancestor and the purity of the callee are all facts the substrate already carries -- so a check can refuse a file whose claims each re-derive one shared pure precondition above a threshold, and report the multiplicity rather than the total. It is not structurally impossible, because the invalid state remains perfectly authorable: nothing stops a claim from calling a pure function that a sibling claim also calls, and that shape is correct whenever the value is cheap. The defect is a cost property of an otherwise legitimate construction, so it is refusable but not unconstructible. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: the floor reports, for each refusing file, the shared pure preconditions its claims re-derive and the multiplicity -- sufficient that a cost refusal names the duplication where one exists, so the reader is never offered trim-or-re-home as an exhaustive choice over work that should have been computed once. Until then the class is found by partitioning a claim by hand, which requires an author who already suspects it. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
